        "root_concepts": "[overview]",
        "section": "criminology",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Criminology - Landscape and Taxonomy",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\n1700s   ENLIGHTENMENT / CLASSICAL\n        Beccaria (1764), Bentham (1789)\n        Crime as rational choice; punishment as deterrence\n               |\n               v\n1890s   POSITIVIST / BIOLOGICAL\n        Lombroso -- atavistic criminal type (now discredited)\n        Ferri -- social factors matter too\n               |\n               v\n1920s   CHICAGO SCHOOL (Ecological)\n        Park, Burgess, Shaw, McKay\n        Crime as product of urban disorganization\n               |\n        +------+--------+\n        |               |\n        v               v\n1938    STRAIN/ANOMIE   DIFFERENTIAL ASSOCIATION\n        Merton          Sutherland\n        Blocked goals   Criminal learning in groups\n        |               |\n        v               v\n1960s   LABELING        WHITE-COLLAR\n        Lemert, Becker  Sutherland expands\n        Deviance is     Corporate crime redefined\n        constructed\n        |\n        v\n1969    SOCIAL CONTROL\n        Hirschi -- bonds to society prevent crime\n        |\n        v\n1979    ROUTINE ACTIVITY\n        Cohen & Felson -- opportunity structure\n        |\n        v\n1990s   LIFE-COURSE / DESISTANCE\n        Sampson & Laub -- turning points\n        |\n        v\n2000s   BIOSOCIAL / INTEGRATED\n        Genetic x environment interactions\n        Neurological correlates\n        |\n        v\n2010s+  ALGORITHMIC JUSTICE / DIGITAL\n        Predictive policing, algorithmic bail\n        Cybercrime, dark web, cryptocurrency\n```"
    },
